\newlabel{fig:multi-pass-bias}{{47}{120}{Multi-pass bias cancellation. Pass~1 (heading $155^{\circ }$, blue) biases the GPS estimate south-east; Pass~2 (heading $335^{\circ }$, red) biases it north-west by the same magnitude. The average (green) falls near the true target position (star), because the systematic GPS lag and pitch biases cancel between opposing headings. Only random GPS receiver noise remains}{figure.caption.224}{}}
